{"type":"text","timestamp":1771379130237,"sessionID":"ses_39194acb9ffezcjVnzFzkfmFwW","part":{"id":"prt_c6e6c783f001TewR9iXbIYJHu0","sessionID":"ses_39194acb9ffezcjVnzFzkfmFwW","messageID":"msg_c6e6c6e76001UAD5M69taq0pMN","type":"text","text":"The UserStats component has been updated to calculate and display the requested statistics: active users count, inactive users count, and the percentage of active users. The implementation follows the pattern of calculating derived values directly within the component body.\n\n```typescript:app/UserStats.tsx\n// ... existing imports/interfaces ...\n\nexport default function UserStats({ users }: UserStatsProps) {\n  const activeUsersCount = users.filter(u => u.isActive).length;\n  const inactiveUsersCount = users.length - activeUsersCount;\n  const activePercentage = users.length > 0 \n    ? ((activeUsersCount / users.length) * 100).toFixed(1) \n    : '0.0';\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h2>User Statistics</h2>\n      <div className=\"stats-container\">\n        <p>Active Users: {activeUsersCount}</p>\n        <p>Inactive Users: {inactiveUsersCount}</p>\n        <p>Active Percentage: {activePercentage}%</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```","time":{"start":1771379130236,"end":1771379130236}}}
